  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "The world's largest gold coin has a mass of about $1\\,\\text{ton}.$  What is this mass in pounds?",
  "worked_solution": "A table showing the customary units of mass is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Ton | $\\text{ton}$ | $1\\,\\text{ton}=2,000\\,\\text{lb}$ |\n| Pound | $\\text{lb}$ | $1\\,\\text{lb}=16\\,\\text{oz}$ |\n| Ounce | $\\text{oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\text{ton}$ is equivalent to $2,000\\,\\text{lb}.$",
